    "description": "A collection of four antique 14K yellow gold jewelry pieces displaying fine period craftsmanship, openwork decoration, seed pearls, enamel, and carved carnelian.\\n\\n* Seed Pearl and Gemstone Brooch: An elaborate winged design embellished with seed pearls, blue stones, and two bezel-set colorless stones. Finished with a delicate safety chain. Stamped “14K.” Measures approximately 30 mm at the center and weighs 3.16 grams.\\n* Carnelian Cameo Intaglio Pendant: An oval reddish-orange carnelian carved with a classical figural scene. The design is carved into the stone in the intaglio technique and surrounded by applied bead and ropework decoration. Stamped “14K.” The stone measures approximately 16.1  13.3 mm. Pendant weighs 3.92 grams.\\n* Seed Pearl Floral Drop Brooch: An openwork circular floral design accented with seed pearls and suspended from an elongated geometric bar.\\n* Enamel Lyre Brooch: A petite lyre-form design with pale green enamel, seed pearl accents, and a bezel-set golden-colored stone.\\n* Combined weight: 8.89 grams\\n\\nThe exact identities of the blue, colorless, and golden-colored stones have not been confirmed. Some seed pearls display age-related wear and losses. Please review all photographs for condition and completeness.\\n\\n\nReviewed and certified by a GIA-certified gemologist. Shippable; $25 minimum shipping. Please review the terms and conditions for all details.",
